  "goodToKnow": "Das Wintersemester (WS or WiSe) is the winter semester at German universities, running from October to March, with lectures roughly mid-October to mid-February; das Sommersemester (SoSe) runs April to September. Most degree courses start in the Wintersemester. Students count their progress in semesters: im fünften Semester. The break is die vorlesungsfreie Zeit or Semesterferien. Plural: die Wintersemester."
